- @next: President Ronald Reagan has won a landslide victory, securing a second term in office.

@next

His Democratic rival Walter Mondale suffered a crushing defeat, carrying only his home state of Minnesota and the District of Columbia. The Republicans swept nearly the entire country.

Overall this means a continuation of the Reagan administration's hardline anti-communist foreign policy and economic conservatism, with the scale of this victory likely to embolden Reagan to pursue his domestic and international objectives with even less restraint.